The colorlist command displays all of the possible color combinations
on DarkWind.  Here is a short explanation of how to create those
combinations:

Color codes are used by typing |<code> where you'd like the color to
begin and | XX0 where it should stop.  Do not include a space between
the | and the code, it is included in this document so you can see
the codes.

The first letter of the code denotes the foreground color.  Acceptable
colors are:
  R   red
  G   green
  B   blue
  K   black
  Y   yellow
  C   cyan
  W   white
  M   magenta

The second letter of the code denotes the background.  The acceptable
colors are the same as the foreground list.

The third letter of the code denotes the affect.
Acceptable options are:
  B   bold
  U   underscore
  K   blinking
  0   no affect

A few examples:
The code | XR0 produces |XR0This|XX0.
The code | BYK produces |BYKThis|XX0.
The code | GKB produces |GKBThis|XX0.
